chology Sustainability & Environmental Studies Workshops Entrepreneurship Week Vision to Venture Winfield Start-Up Showdown Event Business Partner Information Upcoming Events Access Resources Photo Gallery Directory Student Services : Center for Career & Vocation Center for Career & Vocation Schedule an Appointment The Future Is Yours to Build. We Can Help. The Center for Career & Vocation is located in Deets Library, across from the Stir & Bustle coffee shop. Career services include: Career and discernment navigation Job searching and networking skills Resume writing assistance Application assistance Interview preparation Career readiness workshops Our VISION: Inspire students to be excited about their career goals and future and empower lifetime learning and personal vocational growth through meaningful career experiences. Our MISSION: Provide career focused meaningful experiences to help students: Explore career interests, values, passions, career options, and personal vocational discernment. Engage in purposeful internship and job experiences to gain valuable career skills and knowledge. Design and accomplish ongoing career goals. Navigate mentoring connections and partnerships with a variety of businesses, stakeholders, and alumni. The Center for Career & Vocation now has an Instagram page...follow along at sc_careerservices View this post on Instagram A post shared by Carey Keller (@sc_careerservices) A post shared by Carey Keller (@sc_careerservices) Fall 2026 Career Expo's There will be a Career Expo and the date is listed below. It will be in Deets Library from 11:00pm-2:30pm. Date TBD Current List of Businesses coming will be updated as registrations start coming in: Business Administration Education Criminal Justice and Legal Studies Accounting Agribusiness Health Science Communications Psychology Sciences (Biology Chemistry Biochem) Computer Science Does your business want an exhibit at one of the Career Expo's? Businesses are invited to attend and provide a hands-on activity or demonstration pertaining to a career or careers plus provide pertinent information such as career opportunities at their business or in their career field, career outlook, etc. Information may be provided through a variety of ways such as signage, displays, or handouts. Exhibitor Booth Registration Schedule an Appointment Carey Keller Director – Center for Career and Vocation Stop in for an appointment or sign up below! CLICK HERE Build a life Students are what make Student Life happen! From carnivals to concerts, from Sutton Center to Campus Life, the Office of Student Affairs is available for you, the student. learn more about student life Contact us. Who Are You? Future Student Current Student Faculty & Staff Alumni & Friends Parents & Families Who We Are. Site Map Accreditation Privacy Policy Visit Professional Studies What You're Looking For. About SC Academics Activities Administrative Offices Admissions Alumni Affiliated Institutes Athletics Campus Tour Employment At SC FAQs Halls of Fame Homecoming Helpful Forms & Links History Library Mission News Photo Galleries Quick Facts Refer a Student Registrar SC Merchandise Social Media Student Life Student Services The Southwesterner Traditions Transcripts Update Your Information Upcoming Events Webcasts Yearbook Archive Questions? We can help. Send us an email. email sc SC is a United Methodist affiliated college. Southwestern College is a 501(c)(3) organization qualified under Internal Revenue Code Section 170(b)(1)(A). \nFederal Tax ID: 48-0543715. Facebook Youtube Instagram 100 College Street Winfield, KS 67156-2499 1-800-846-1543 message Maps & directions ©2026 SOUTHWESTERN COLLEGE ‹ › ×"
